{"dur":120,"ev":[{"t":1.8,"type":"voice","id":"v01"},{"t":7.6,"type":"voice","id":"v02"},{"t":19.2,"type":"voice","id":"v03"},{"t":32.4,"type":"voice","id":"v04"},{"t":39.2,"type":"voice","id":"v05"},{"t":50.8,"type":"voice","id":"v06"},{"t":54.25,"type":"voice","id":"i1"},{"t":57.85,"type":"voice","id":"i2"},{"t":61.45,"type":"voice","id":"i3"},{"t":65.05,"type":"voice","id":"i4"},{"t":72.2,"type":"voice","id":"v07"},{"t":86.8,"type":"voice","id":"v08"},{"t":103.4,"type":"voice","id":"v09"},{"t":1.8,"type":"sub","d":5.063,"text":"Long ago, the gods had grown weak, and they turned to Vishnu for help."},{"t":7.6,"type":"sub","d":6.368,"text":"Go and churn the ocean of milk, he told them, and it will give you the nectar of immortality."},{"t":19.2,"type":"sub","d":9.337,"text":"So they made a mountain their churning rod, and the serpent Vasuki their rope. Gods on one side, demons on the other, they pulled."},{"t":32.4,"type":"sub","d":2.3290000000000006,"text":"But the mountain began to sink."},{"t":39.2,"type":"sub","d":5.832999999999998,"text":"So Vishnu became Kurma, a great tortoise, and carried the mountain on his back."},{"t":50.8,"type":"sub","d":3.286999999999999,"text":"The ocean turned, and gave up its treasures."},{"t":54.1,"type":"sub","d":14.100000000000001,"text":"The moon. A white elephant. A tree that grants every wish. A cow of plenty."},{"t":72.2,"type":"sub","d":9.090999999999994,"text":"Then, standing on a lotus, came Lakshmi, the goddess of fortune. She looked at the gods and the demons, and she chose Vishnu."},{"t":86.8,"type":"sub","d":5.8160000000000025,"text":"Last of all rose the healer of the gods, holding a pot of amrita, the nectar."},{"t":103.4,"type":"sub","d":6.744,"text":"This is the churning of the ocean: how the world was steadied, on the patient back of a tortoise."},{"t":0.3,"type":"baren","g":0},{"t":0.72,"type":"baren","g":1},{"t":1.14,"type":"baren","g":2},{"t":1.56,"type":"baren","g":3},{"t":15.8,"type":"baren","g":0},{"t":16.2